.TH AVR\-ORG\-INSTALL\-RUNNER\-CREATE 1 "" "avr 0.5.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-org-install-runner-create \- Create group runners in GitLab and configure their machine types in Avrea.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr org install runner create
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create group runners in GitLab and configure their machine types in Avrea.
.PP
Supply your own personal access token with create_runner scope and Owner role. It is sent only to gitlab.com and is never persisted. Already configured machine types must be replaced with 'runner set'.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    data, setup
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-installation\-id\fR \fITEXT\fR
GitLab installation ID (ins-xxx format). (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-machine\-type\fR \fITEXT\fR
Machine type to create; repeat for multiple machine types. (repeatable; required)
.TP
\fB\-\-protected\fR
Restrict the runners to protected branches and tags.
.TP
\fB\-\-personal\-access\-token\-stdin\fR
Read your personal access token from standard input instead of a hidden prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-org-install-runner (1),
.BR avr-org-install-runner-delete (1),
.BR avr-org-install-runner-list (1),
.BR avr-org-install-runner-set (1)
